@startuml
title TMFC010 : Resource Catalog Management -- eTOM/SID ABE Links

class "L2 - Resource Catalog Lifecycle Management" as L2Lifecycle <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "L2 - Resource Catalog Operational Readiness Management" as L2OperReadiness <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "L2 - Resource Catalog Content Management" as L2Content <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "L2 - Resource Catalog Planning Management" as L2Planning <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "L2 - Resource Specification Management" as L2SpecMgmt <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "L2 - Resource Specification Development & Retirement" as L2DevRetirement <<eTOM Business Activity>>

class "Resource Specification ABE" as SIDSpec <<SID Data Entity>>
class "Resource Usage ABE" as SIDUsage <<SID Data Entity>>
class "Resource Performance ABE" as SIDPerformance <<SID Data Entity>>
class "Resource Configuration ABE" as SIDConfiguration <<SID Data Entity>>

' Per the image's own legend: a (black) arrow from an eTOM activity towards a
' SID ABE means the information is produced by the activity; the reverse
' arrow means the information is consumed by the activity. The source image
' also draws some of these same eTOM<->SID connections in red and cyan
' instead of black -- the legend does not assign the colors any separate
' meaning, so they are treated here purely as a visual grouping style and
' the produces/consumed-by labeling still follows arrow direction alone.

' Resource Specification ABE has four direct eTOM connections, each drawn
' individually (not through the shared trunk described below):
L2Lifecycle --> SIDSpec : produces
SIDSpec --> L2Lifecycle : is consumed by

' Only a single arrow is drawn between Resource Specification ABE and
' Operational Readiness Management (ABE -> activity) -- reproduced as a
' single direction exactly as drawn, with no reverse arrow invented.
SIDSpec --> L2OperReadiness : is consumed by

L2SpecMgmt --> SIDSpec : produces
SIDSpec --> L2SpecMgmt : is consumed by

' Likewise only a single arrow is drawn between Resource Specification ABE
' and Planning Management (ABE -> activity).
SIDSpec --> L2Planning : is consumed by

' Resource Catalog Content Management and Resource Specification Development
' & Retirement each connect to all four SID ABEs via a single shared vertical
' "bus" line in the source image: one arrowhead branches off toward each of
' the four ABEs (produces), while the reverse, consumed-by direction is drawn
' as a single merged arrowhead back into the activity box rather than as four
' separate arrowheads. The relationship is reproduced here as fully
' bidirectional for each of the four ABEs, per the legend's direction-based
' meaning, with this shared-bus economy noted for transparency.
L2Content --> SIDSpec : produces
SIDSpec --> L2Content : is consumed by
L2Content --> SIDUsage : produces
SIDUsage --> L2Content : is consumed by
L2Content --> SIDPerformance : produces
SIDPerformance --> L2Content : is consumed by
L2Content --> SIDConfiguration : produces
SIDConfiguration --> L2Content : is consumed by

L2DevRetirement --> SIDSpec : produces
SIDSpec --> L2DevRetirement : is consumed by
L2DevRetirement --> SIDUsage : produces
SIDUsage --> L2DevRetirement : is consumed by
L2DevRetirement --> SIDPerformance : produces
SIDPerformance --> L2DevRetirement : is consumed by
L2DevRetirement --> SIDConfiguration : produces
SIDConfiguration --> L2DevRetirement : is consumed by

@enduml
